arm64: give libbpf the 128-bit types the shadowing hides

The 7.3 line builds libbpf 1.6.2 against the kernel's exported uapi
headers, and that fails:

    staging_dir/toolchain-aarch64_cortex-a53_gcc-14.3.0_musl/include/asm/ptrace.h:96:9:
        error: unknown type name '__u128'; did you mean '__u32'?

Why it fails, and why 6.18 does not:

  * libbpf's src/Makefile puts -I../include and -I../include/uapi in front
    of every system directory, and libbpf ships its own include/linux/types.h.
  * the exported uapi linux/ptrace.h and the exported uapi asm/ptrace.h both
    include <linux/types.h>, which therefore resolves to libbpf's copy - and
    that copy has no __u128.
  * the 7.3.4 arm64 asm/ptrace.h uses __u128 (struct user_fpsimd_state, the
    PAC key structures), and the only place the exported uapi headers define
    __u128 is linux/types.h - the copy that is shadowed.
  * 6.18's arm64 asm/ptrace.h spells the same fields __uint128_t, and that
    name is visible to user space, so the 6.18 line builds libbpf fine.
    (Its published initramfs carries usr/lib/libbpf.so.1 and libbpf.so.1.6.2,
    so the 6.18 line really does build it.)

One more thing rides on the same shadowing, but it is not a build error:
the exported uapi linux/swab.h uses __attribute_const__, which the kernel
defines in its own compiler attributes header - a header it does not export.
The kernel's scripts/headers_install.sh strips the macro out of every header
it exports (scripts/headers_install.sh:34), so the headers libbpf really
compiles against do not carry it either - and the CI's diagnostic pass did not
report a single __attribute_const__ error, only the six __u128 ones.

So __attribute_const__ is defined here only as a guarded fallback: it is the
kernel's own spelling, wrapped in #ifndef, so it costs nothing when the macro
is already there and saves the build if a header ever stops being stripped.
The build does not need it.

So the definitions go into the copy of linux/types.h that libbpf actually
compiles against: __u128 and __s128 are copied verbatim from the kernel's uapi
linux/types.h, and __attribute_const__ is the kernel's own spelling, guarded.

This patch lives in overlays-73/ only: the 6.18 release line does not get
it, and does not need it.

--- a/include/linux/types.h
+++ b/include/linux/types.h
@@ -11,6 +11,15 @@
 
 #include <asm/types.h>
 #include <asm/posix_types.h>
+
+#ifdef __SIZEOF_INT128__
+typedef __signed__ __int128 __s128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+typedef unsigned __int128 __u128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+#endif
+
+#ifndef __attribute_const__
+#define __attribute_const__ __attribute__((__const__))
+#endif
 
 #define __bitwise__
 #define __bitwise __bitwise__
